## Objective
- Perform adversarial round-1 review of phase-097 ("parse and format dates from text") in the redblue checkout, reporting only genuinely wrong behaviour in the mandated `FINDINGS:` format plus a final `REVIEW VERDICT:` line.

## Important Details
- Reviewer is READ-ONLY: `bash`, `edit`, `task`, etc. denied; must reason from files/tests. Cannot run cargo/git.
- Contract requires: every finding cites `file:line` actually read; severity ∈ `BLOCKER|MAJOR|MINOR|STYLE`; every BLOCKER needs a `VERIFIED:` marker (else downgrade to MAJOR); check for existing tests that pin claimed-broken behaviour before reporting; do not pad.
- Output must end with exactly `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`; zero findings is valid (`FINDINGS: none` + `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`).
- Phase changes: ISO-8601 `time.parse`, date-aware `time.format`/`time.unix`, `nanosecond` date property, shared `date_text` printer (`%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S%.f`), fractional `time.unix`, legacy `time.unix` layout fallback, truncation of numeric instants.
- Uncommitted changes revert round-1's floor change back to truncation toward zero in `seconds_for_instant`; REPORT/SPEC now document `time.from_unix(-0.5)` = `1970-01-01 00:00:00`, `-1.9` = `1969-12-31 23:59:59`; existing phase-096 test `edge_time_from_unix_truncates_a_fractional_second_like_time_format` was restored. This is compatibility-correct (pre-phase code was `timestamp as i64`); tests pin it, so do not report as a defect.
- Known/documented asymmetry: `time.unix(parse("1969-12-31T23:59:59.5Z"))` = `-0.5` but `time.from_unix(-0.5)` = epoch; listed in REPORT known gaps; document is self-consistent.
- Registry facts verified: 85 builtins (`src/stdlib.rs:1165`–`1250`), 63 dotted members (`src/stdlib.rs:63`), `time.parse` registered/member/signature (`src/stdlib.rs:460`, `1214`, `1393`).
- Gate table claims fmt/clippy pass, `cargo test --all-targets` 2279 passed, `../rbops/verify.sh phase-097` pass — unverifiable read-only.

