FINDINGS:
- [MAJOR] `src/runtime.rs:929` — the `checked_sub_signed` refusal for an offset that moves a valid edge date outside chrono's calendar range has no test; the out-of-window tests use offset-free texts (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:296-303`, `src/runtime.rs:2903-2926`) and the offset tests use ordinary 2024 dates (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:888`). A regression here would be silent. Fix: add a catchable-error test for `time.parse("-262143-01-01T00:00:00+01:00")` (and the symmetric maximum).
- [MAJOR] `src/runtime.rs:1000` — the true side of `seconds > MAX_SECONDS` in `unix_seconds_for` is untested; every out-of-window test is negative (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:298`), and positive tests stop at `+10000` equality (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:337`, `:1082`). Fix: add `time.unix(time.parse("+10001-01-01"))` as a catchable `time.unix` refusal in `edge_time_unix_refuses_a_fraction_past_the_positive_window_edge` or a sibling test.
- [MINOR] `SURVEY.md:269` — cites `src/runtime.rs:1704` for "formats a date or a numeric timestamp", but 1704 is `time.sleep`'s `sleep_for`; `time.format` begins at `src/runtime.rs:1708`. Update the citation to 1708.
- [MINOR] `src/runtime.rs:545` — `seconds_for_format`'s doc says a timestamp that is "not whole" is a `Runtime` error, but `seconds_for_instant` accepts and truncates fractional timestamps, as pinned by `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:763`. Update the doc to say fractional timestamps truncate toward zero rather than adding the refusal.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
